[["page","lines",76],{"text":"The UPLC-ESI-QTOF-MS analysis led to the tentative detec-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":227.3595899999999,"width":240.9352377599999,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",77],{"text":"tion of 108 compounds in urine, including some native phe-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":238.3129399999999,"width":240.95048063999997,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",78],{"text":"nolics present in the capsule, their phase-II derived metabo-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":249.2752599999999,"width":240.93882431999992,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",79],{"text":"lites, and also from microbial origin. From all these compounds,","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":260.23758,"width":240.9164083199999,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",80],{"text":"84 were detected in plasma, and 49 compounds reached NT","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":271.19093999999996,"width":240.9397209600001,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",81],{"text":"and 47 MT (Table S4, Supporting Information). All these com-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":282.15325999999993,"width":240.9451007999998,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",82],{"text":"pounds were derived from isoflavones (38 metabolites), curcum-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":293.11557999999997,"width":240.96034368,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",83],{"text":"inoids (16 metabolites), lignans (26 metabolites), resveratrol (18","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":304.06892999999997,"width":240.97200000000004,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",84],{"text":"metabolites), and low-molecular-weight phenolic metabolites (10","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":315.03124999999994,"width":240.92985791999985,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",85],{"text":"metabolites) (Table S4, Supporting Information). For all the com-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":325.9935699999999,"width":240.93972095999987,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",86],{"text":"pounds, molecular formulas were obtained with a high score","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":336.94692999999995,"width":240.95944704000016,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",87],{"text":"(<90) and low error (3 ppm) (Table S4, Supporting Information).","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":347.90924999999993,"width":240.9397192799999,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",88],{"text":"According to the patients’ food questionnaires, their normal diet","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":358.87156999999996,"width":240.95317055999993,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",89],{"text":"and the food items consumed 24 h before the surgery by the","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":369.82491999999996,"width":240.9433075199999,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",90],{"text":"patients did not present sources of isoflavones, curcuminoids,","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":380.78723999999994,"width":240.93523776,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",91],{"text":"resveratrol, and lignans. In contrast, the consumption of coffee,","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":391.7406,"width":240.9495839999999,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",92],{"text":"bread, cereals, and other plant food sources could explain the low-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":402.70291999999995,"width":240.93703104000002,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",93],{"text":"molecular-weight metabolites’ presence. This was confirmed in","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":413.6652399999999,"width":240.92358143999985,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",94],{"text":"the control patients, where these low-molecular-weight phenolics","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":424.6185899999999,"width":240.92089152,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",95],{"text":"were detected but not those metabolites derived from isoflavones,","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":435.58090999999996,"width":240.92447808000014,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",96],{"text":"curcuminoids, resveratrol, and lignans.","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.0909,"y":446.54323999999997,"width":147.71068032,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",97],{"text":"Table 2 shows the polyphenols and their derived metabo-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":312.55852,"y":457.49658999999997,"width":231.46760967999995,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",98],{"text":"lites quantified in urine, plasma, and mammary tissues. Those","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":468.45890999999995,"width":240.93075456000003,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",99],{"text":"metabolites with no authentic standards were tentatively identi-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":479.4212299999999,"width":240.9585504000001,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",100],{"text":"fied (Table S4, Supporting Information) but not quantified be-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":490.37458999999996,"width":240.93703104000002,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",101],{"text":"cause the signal in UPLC-ESI-QTOF was significantly different","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":501.33690999999993,"width":240.96034368,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",102],{"text":"depending on the metabolite and type of conjugation. Figure 2","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":512.29923,"width":240.94510312000006,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",103],{"text":"shows representative EICs of quantified compounds in mam-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":523.25258,"width":240.95496383999983,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",104],{"text":"mary tissues (NT and MT), urine, and plasma from a BC patient.","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":534.2149,"width":240.94061759999983,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",105],{"text":"As expected, high interindividual variability was observed in","fontSize":8.9664,"x":312.55762,"y":545.17722,"width":231.47030591999993,"height":8.966399999999908}]
[["page","lines",106],{"text":"the quantification of phenolics and their derived metabolites","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":556.13058,"width":240.95675711999985,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",107],{"text":"in urine, plasma, and mammary tissues. This variability, to-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":567.0929,"width":240.95675712000008,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",108],{"text":"gether with the lack of standards for the correct quantification","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":578.05522,"width":240.92178816000018,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",109],{"text":"of many metabolites, makes it challenging to obtain full quan-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":589.00857,"width":240.93165119999998,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",110],{"text":"titative conclusions (Table 2). Overall, metabolite concentrations","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":599.9708899999999,"width":240.95855039999987,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",111],{"text":"were higher in NT than MT, although no statistically significant","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":610.9332099999999,"width":240.93254784000027,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",112],{"text":"difference was observed between MT and NT for any metabolite,","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":621.88657,"width":240.9459974400001,"height":8.966399999999908}]
[["page","lines",113],{"text":"including those identified in Table S4, Supporting Information,","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":632.84889,"width":240.94420415999986,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",114],{"text":"when comparing their integrated areas (this approach is not cor-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":643.81121,"width":240.91730495999985,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",115],{"text":"rect for quantification purposes, but it is a valid strategy for com-","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":654.76456,"width":240.95944704000016,"height":8.966400000000021}]
[["page","lines",116],{"text":"paring the abundance of the same specific metabolite in different","fontSize":8.9664,"x":303.09,"y":665.7268799999999,"width":240.96213696,"height":8.966400000000021}]
